{
 "schema": 1,
 "name": "Spirit Culling summons a Spectral Scythe from a generated soul",
 "contract": "Spirit Culling 301986 promises that generating a Reaped Soul has a 10% chance to summon a Spectral Scythe. Its third effect is a SPELL_AURA_PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL for 500576 and its record carries ProcTypeMask 0, so the aura never sees an event; and the event is Ascension's own - a stack of the class's resource aura - so a spell_proc row could not carry it either. The module answers it where it already recognises a newly harvested soul, at the talent's own chance. Souls are awarded in pairs, one spent and one generated, because Reaped Soul holds three stacks and a grant at the cap is not a generation. Eighty generations make a run where a 10% talent never fires 0.9^80, under a hundredth of one per cent.",
 "timeout_ms": 180000,
